The trim-cpanfile commit 8d3017f dropped the explicit requires for core modules and with them two ADR-pointer comments the pre-release audit flagged as lost context: B -> File::SOPS::Encrypted::detect_type + docs/adr/0002 (IOK/NOK flag reading for type detection), and Math::BigFloat -> docs/adr/0006 (the only measured carrier that writes a 16-17 digit double as a bare number the MAC covers). Not a defect -- both core under perl 5.014 -- and the trim was deliberate, so this is a maintainer judgment call: restoring the doc value means re-adding requires+comments (undoing the trim for those two), or leaving the pointers only in the ADRs. Tracked so it is not lost; no auto-fix. Also dropped: File::Temp and Text::ParseWords rationale comments.

Maintainer-Entscheidung (getty): B und Math::BigFloat sind Core seit perl 5.014, gehoeren nicht in die cpanfile -- der Trim (8d3017f) war richtig, kein Dependency-Problem. Verlorene ADR-Zeiger-Kommentare bleiben in ADR 0002 (B/detect_type) und ADR 0006 (Math::BigFloat) erhalten; kein Wiederherstellen in der cpanfile. Als done geschlossen.
